> Now sessions from subdirectories are appearing in the parent directory, which is very bad and incompatible. I think it's a bug.

I submitted https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/pull/31210 which should restore the behavior for cases outside of what this PR intended to address (it did so too broadly and roped in non-git cases).

@jlongster please review https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/pull/31210 as it refines the scope of your earlier PR - it's led to a string of issues and even cases where users may continue a session context from within its parent folder, which can lead to edits outside of the intended `external_directory` of that session).

I have tested this and found that the corret option is
```
"models": {
        "MiniMax-M3": {
          "reasoning": true,
          "variants": {
            "none": {
              "thinking": {
                "type": "disabled"
              }
            },
            "think":{
              "thinking": {
                "type": "adaptive"
              }
